      "problem_text": "If sqrt(28-10sqrt(3)) = sqrt(a)-sqrt(b), find a and b.",
      "answer": "a=25,b=3",
      "solution": "Assume sqrt(28-10sqrt3)=sqrtx-sqrty. Square: x+y-2sqrt(xy)=28-10sqrt3. So x+y=28, 2sqrt(xy)=10sqrt3 => xy=75. x+y=28, xy=75 => x=25,y=3 or x=3,y=25. Since sqrtx > sqrty, sqrt25-sqrt3=5-sqrt3",
