      "problem_text": "Prove that sqrt(2) is irrational.",
      "answer": "Proof",
      "solution": "Assume sqrt2=p/q in lowest terms. Then 2=p^2/q^2 => 2q^2=p^2. So p^2 even => p even => p=2k => 2q^2=4k^2 => q^2=2k^2 => q even. So p,q both even, contradiction as fraction was reduced.",
